Native language tooling update
-------------------------------
The package now includes mojo-lsp-server, with 12 passing upstream protocol
regressions and one upstream-disabled definition test. Nine more CPU
documentation targets pass, including all three manual decorator examples.
The six Support configuration tests also pass. A fresh unpack passes language-
server initialization and all 93 Python cases with rebuilt Python 3.12.15.
Clean VM lifecycle checks and the fresh end-to-end build remain in progress.
See README.mojo-tests.5BSD for separate-run counts and remaining gaps.

Package archive verification update (2026-10-09)
-----------------------------------------------
An initial repackaging invocation discarded generated plist entries, omitting
Mojo examples and most JDK files. The procedure now restages and packages
without deleting that generated list. The corrected archives match every
staged file: Mojo 26, JDK 519, Python 8029 and Bazel 5. JDK Java registration
hooks are present. Corrected Mojo examples, CPU counts and both ASan diagnostic
modes pass. Evidence: package-file-coverage.json, language-tools-package/ and
openjdk21-complete-manifest-package.log under the validation directory.
The earlier incomplete archive hashes are retained as failure evidence.

Formatter qualification (2026-10-09)
-----------------------------------
The port now includes upstream's pure-Python mblack formatter, resolved by
`mojo format` inside the private SDK. It uses existing native/noarch Python
ports rather than downloaded runtime wheels. All five dependency packages
build and pass stage QA and plist checks without host installation.
The complete upstream formatter suite passes 1004 tests with two explicit
upstream skips: one obsolete Click-internal API check and one Python-stub-only
case. The two broken config-discovery mocks now use real temporary project
configs and check their effect on formatting. Test-only patches accommodate current Click's
separate stdout API, enable filesystem tests outside Bazel and restore missing
file-discovery fixtures/renamed ignore patterns. No formatter algorithm was
changed. Optional compile-every-sample validation is in progress. The earlier development package passes directory formatting, idempotence, cache selection,
compilation/execution of formatted Mojo, invalid-input and syntax-error checks.
Its archive matches every staged file and records all seven direct runtime
dependencies; stage QA and plist checks pass. This is the development compiler
package. The independent fresh-source compiler build has now completed.
Evidence: /usr/obj/mojo-port-validation/2026-10-09/formatter/.

Virtual CPU qualification update (2026-10-09)
--------------------------------------------
The four-vCPU/two-domain QEMU `max` run passes all 40 BaseTest and 18 WorkQueue
tests, but compiling the packaged operators example fails with LLVM's
"64-bit code requested on a subtarget that doesn't support it" diagnostic.
The guest reports AuthenticAMD family 6/model 6 alongside long-mode and AVX2
features. The default synthetic CPU is therefore not qualified. A named
Haswell-noTSX four-vCPU/two-domain retry is in progress; this changes only the
test VM, not base, the port's default compilation flags or the host. The full
package lifecycle and sixteen-vCPU compiler checks remain incomplete.
Evidence: language-tools-four-cpu-result.json and serial-language-tools-four-cpu.log
under /usr/obj/mojo-qualification-vm/. Never infer a pass from QEMU exit status
alone: this failed run shut down cleanly with process status zero.

